NEXT TEST: Test 1, run 2: voice capture with 2 people (docs/LIVE_TEST.md)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Why
  Run 1 had only the DM, so consent revoke and two speakers weren't tested. Since then
  a lot has landed on development, and run 2 is its first live check:
    - Postgres storage (#68), shard-ready startup and JSON logs (#69)
    - /dmbot start . stop . help . backup . restore, with campaigns (#47, #48)
    - DM screen made automatically, named #dmb-dm-screen-<campaign> (#30, #87)
    - picking a session back up after a restart (#70)
    - the audio-pause fix from run 1 (#36)
  Passing run 2 is what lets development be promoted to beta.

Before the test (owner)
  [ ] Postgres set up on the PC, once (README, "Database"); DATABASE_URL in .env
  [ ] Compare .env with .env.example and add anything missing (#31)
  [ ] .env: TRANSCRIBER=none and DMBOT_DEBUG_AUDIO=1
  [ ] A second person in the voice channel (a phone with a second account is fine)
  [ ] Optional: the "clumsy" tool (Windows) to add ~5% packet loss

Before the test (PyCharm session)
  [ ] Follow LIVE_TEST.md steps 2-3 (pull development, pg_ctl start, pip install,
      npm ci); confirm "ears connected"

Commands to use
  /dmbot start, /consent give, /consent revoke, /dmbot help (Status), /dmbot stop
  (/table join and /table status are gone)

What to check (in addition to LIVE_TEST.md step 5)
  - /dmbot start creates #dmb-dm-screen-<campaign> with a help card
  - Debug line per utterance in the ears terminal (pauses=..., link_dropped_total=0)
  - Long sentences with short pauses read 95-100%; with ~5% loss injected the % drops
  - The second person's /consent revoke removes them from the next capture checks
  - The ⚠️ flag, not the rounded %, decides pass or fail (#44)
  - Optional extra: stop core with Ctrl+C mid-session and start it again. DMbot should
    rejoin and post a note in the DM screen (#70)

